{title: Deck the Halls}
{key: D}
{time: 4/4}

[D]Deck the halls [A7]with [Bm]boughs [A]of [D]holly,
[A7]Fa la la la [D]la, la la [A]la [D]la.
[D]'Tis the sea[A7]son [Bm]to [A]be [D]jolly,
[A7]Fa la la la [D]la, la la [A]la [D]la.
[A]Don we [A7]now our [D]gay ap[A]parel,
[D]Fa la la, [Bm]la la la, [A]la [E7]la [A]la.
[D]Troll the an[A]cient [Bm]Yule[A]tide [D]carol,
[G]Fa la la la [D]la, la la [A7]la [D]la.

See the blazing Yule before us,
Fa la la la la, la la la la.
Strike the harp and join the chorus,
Fa la la la la, la la la la.
Follow me in merry measure,
Fa la la, la la la, la la la.
While I tell of Yuletide treasure,
Fa la la la la, la la la la.

Fast away the old year passes,
Fa la la la la, la la la la.
Hail the new, ye lads and lasses,
Fa la la la la, la la la la.
Sing we joyous all together,
Fa la la, la la la, la la la.
Heedless of the wind and weather,
Fa la la la la, la la la la.
